  In order to get GCC on my system to compile properly, I had to make the
following patch to system.h:

*** OLDsystem.h Fri Sep  8 14:17:24 1989
--- system.h    Fri Sep  8 14:59:39 1989
***************
*** 12,17 ****
--- 12,21 ----
  typedef unsigned int  size_t;
  #else
  # include <sys/types.h>
+ # ifdef __GNUC__
+ #  undef NULL
+ #  include <stddef.h>
+ # endif
  #endif

  #ifdef ULTRIX


If I didn't do this, GCC reported parse errors because size_t was undefined.
This may not happen in general, but if you have any problems with compiling
Nethack 3.0 on GCC, try this patch. 

